==English==
{{was wotd|2016|January|16}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From the phrase ''by [[hear]] [[say]]'', a translation of {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|fr|[[par#French|par]] [[ouïr]] [[dire#French|dire]]|}} (1525–1535).

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-hearsay.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|hear|say|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[information|Information]] that was [[heard]] by one [[person]] about [[another]] that cannot be adequately substantiated.
# {{lb|en|law}} [[evidence|Evidence]] based on the [[report]]s of others rather than on [[personal]] [[knowledge]], which is normally [[inadmissible]] because it was not made under [[oath]].
# {{lb|en|law}} An out-of-court statement offered in court for the truth of the matter asserted, which is normally inadmissible because it is not subject to [[cross-examination]] unless the hearsay statement falls under one of a number of [[exception]]s.

